<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Parla — Apple Privacy Manifest (iOS app target).

  Parla is 100% on-device: it transcribes audio/video to text locally with WhisperKit and never
  sends user content anywhere. Hence:
    • NSPrivacyTracking            = false   (no tracking, no ATT)
    • NSPrivacyTrackingDomains     = []      (no domains contacted for tracking)
    • NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes  = []      (we collect NOTHING — no analytics, no accounts)
    • NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes    = UserDefaults + FileTimestamp

  UserDefaults (CA92.1): the app stores its OWN preferences (selected model, UI language, toggles,
  dictation options) in UserDefaults.standard — app-private, never read from other apps or the system,
  never an App Group suite. That is exactly reason CA92.1.

  FileTimestamp (C617.1 — timestamps of files inside the app's own container / its App Group
  container). Two call sites ship in this bundle, both on Parla's own files and never on user-chosen
  documents:
    • apps/ios/Sources/ShareInbox.swift — sweepStaleParts reads .contentModificationDateKey on
      `.part` files in the App Group inbox to clear leftovers from a share the system killed
      mid-copy, without touching one that could still be in flight.
    • ParlaCore/AppModel+History.swift — pruneImportedOrphans reads it on imports/<uuid>/ inside
      Application Support to give a copy that has not been transcribed yet a grace period, so a
      paywalled or retryable import is not deleted out from under the user on the next launch.
  This was previously declared as ABSENT, and the comment asserting that was wrong at the time it was
  written (ShareInbox already read the key). Expect ITMS-91053 on upload until this ships.

  Still deliberately NOT declared, audited against the code in this bundle (ParlaCore + apps/ios/
  Sources + apps/ios/Shared; the macOS-only Sources/Parla is not part of this target): no DiskSpace,
  no SystemBootTime, no ActiveKeyboards. The bundled xcframeworks (opus, ogg) and WhisperKit's deps
  (swift-transformers, swift-crypto) carry their OWN PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy inside their frameworks;
  the two app extensions carry theirs under Extensions/{Share,Widgets}.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
    <false/>
    <key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
    <array/>
    <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
    <array/>
    <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
    <array>
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
            <array>
                <string>CA92.1</string>
            </array>
        </dict>
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
            <array>
                <string>C617.1</string>
            </array>
        </dict>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
